Why does const work in some for-loops in JavaScript?

<p>I <strong>do know</strong> why <code>const</code> doesn't work in for-loops. We need to create a new scope and copy over a value into that. So this won't fly.</p>

<pre><code>for(const i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) console.log(i);
</code></pre>

<p>Whereas this will.</p>

<pre><code>for(let i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++) console.log(i);
