<p>For this, I have created a class that will apply the different parsing rules I have in specified. Getting the parsing rule works fine. I am currently stuck in the actual text transformation/parsing aspect.</p>

<p>Consider I have a parsing rule called "regexTextReplace", that looks like this:</p>

<pre><code>class regexTextReplace
{
    private $pattern;
    private $replacement;

    public function __construct(array $arguments)
    {
        $this-&gt;pattern = $arguments['pattern'];
        $this-&gt;replacement = $arguments['replacement'];
    }

    public function apply(array $table, $column = false): array
    {
        $table = $column ? $table[$column] : $table;

        return array_map('self::regex_replace', $table);
    }

    public function regex_replace(array $table)
    {
        return preg_replace($this-&gt;pattern, $this-&gt;replacement, $table);
    }
}
</code></pre>

