<p>This state is passed on to a <code>Child</code> widget using its constructor.</p>

<p>Now, how I understand it, the <code>Child</code> should get re-built every-time <code>Parent</code>'s state changes, since it's inside the <code>build()</code> function of <code>Parent</code>, and <code>build()</code> gets called every-time the state changes.</p>

<p>This concept lead me to believe that the <code>INIT STATE!</code> message would be printed every time the counter changes. But it is not the case!</p>

<p>I essentially want a "hook" that gets fired only once, whenever the <code>Child</code>'s constructor arguments (<code>message</code>) change.</p>

