Javascript: What is the difference between Function and Class

<p>With the release of ECMAScript 6 on June 2015, Javascript classes syntax was introduced.</p>

<p>This syntax:</p>

<pre><code>class Polygon {
      constructor(width, height) {
        this.width = width;
        this.height = height;
      }
}
</code></pre>

<p>is basically same as:</p>

<pre><code>function Polygon(width, height) {
    this.width = width;
    this.height = height;
}
</code></pre>

<p>So what is the benefit of using class instead of traditional function?
And in what condition I should use class instead of function?</p>

