std::is_floating_point returns false for float in some cases

<p>In some cases, see one example below, <code>std::is_floating_point</code> is returning <code>false</code> for <code>float</code>.</p>

<pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;
#include &lt;type_traits&gt;
#include &lt;vector&gt;

int main()
{
    ::std::cout &lt;&lt; typeid(decltype(::std::vector&lt; float &gt;()[::std::vector&lt; float &gt;().size()])).name() &lt;&lt; ::std::endl;
    if (::std::is_floating_point&lt; decltype(::std::vector&lt; float &gt;()[::std::vector&lt; float &gt;().size()]) &gt;::value)
    {
        ::std::cout &lt;&lt; "floating point" &lt;&lt; ::std::endl;
    }
    else
    {
        ::std::cout &lt;&lt; "not floating point" &lt;&lt; ::std::endl;
    }
    return 0;
}
</code></pre>

<p>Output from GCC</p>

<pre><code>f
not floating point
</code></pre>

<p>In this example, one can see that <code>typeid</code> considers <code>::std::vector&lt; float &gt;()[::std::vector&lt; float &gt;().size()]</code> as a <code>float</code> as it returns the correct name. One can also check that <code>typeid(decltype(::std::vector&lt; float &gt;()[::std::vector&lt; float &gt;().size()])) == typeid(flat)</code> returns <code>true</code>. However, <code>std::is_floating_point</code> is returning false. Why? Is that a bug from C++?</p>

<p>FYI, I checked with both GCC and VisualStudio. In this example, I used std::vector, but one can also try with other libraries, such as Eigen.</p>

